{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uk45AcgGDurRTNvTB5PWfE","type":"tool_result","content":"total 8\ndrwxr-xr-x@  7 anayusta  staff  224 Feb  2 14:56 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  25 anayusta  staff  800 Feb  2 14:53 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  7 anayusta  staff  224 Feb  2 14:55 app\ndrwxr-xr-x@  8 anayusta  staff  256 Feb  2 16:06 components\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 anayusta  staff  160 Feb  2 14:44 i18n\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 anayusta  staff  128 Feb  2 14:42 lib\n-rw-r--r--@  1 anayusta  staff  401 Feb  2 14:56 middleware.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCZ8NHciDs3K8Yn65bPg37","session_id":"bf186ce8-bbc8-474d-8394-9852a20e107e","uuid":"c54c5f17-3df6-491e-8887-69bf66d513e4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCZ8NHciDs3K8Yn65bPg37","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I now have a comprehensive understanding of the authentication implementation. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Authentication Implementation Overview\n\nI've explored your codebase thoroughly. Here's a detailed breakdown of the current authentication setup:\n\n### 1. Project Structure\n\n**Key Directories:**\n- `/src/app/[locale]/login/` - Login page components\n- `/src/app/[locale]/register/` - Registration page components\n- `/src/app/api/auth/check-username/` - Username validation API\n- `/src/app/auth/callback/` - OAuth callback handler\n- `/src/lib/supabase.ts` - Supabase client configuration\n- `/src/components/` - Reusable form components (LoginForm, RegistrationForm)\n- `/supabase/migrations/` - Database schema and setup\n- `/messages/` - Translation files (en.json, es.json)\n\n### 2. Supabase Configuration\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/lib/supabase.ts`\n\nThe Supabase client is initialized with public environment variables:\n- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` - Supabase project URL\n- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` - Anonymous public key\n\nCurrently configured for local development at `http://127.0.0.1:54321` with demo credentials in `.env.local`.\n\n### 3. Database Schema\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202000000_create_profiles_table.sql`\n\n**Profiles Table Structure:**\n```sql\n- id (UUID, references auth.users, primary key)\n- full_name (TEXT, NOT NULL, UNIQUE) - serves as username\n- email (TEXT, optional)\n- created_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)\n- updated_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Row Level Security (RLS) enabled\n- Policies for user profile access (users can view/update own profiles)\n- Public read access for username uniqueness checks\n- Automatic profile creation via trigger on user signup\n- Index on `lower(full_name)` for case-insensitive username lookups\n- Automatic `updated_at` timestamp updates via trigger\n\n### 4. Authentication Flow\n\n#### Registration Flow\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/registration-form.tsx`\n\nFeatures:\n- Form validation using React Hook Form + Zod\n- Full Name (username) validation:\n  - 2-100 characters required\n  - Real-time availability checking with debounce (500ms)\n  - Visual feedback (checking, available, taken icons)\n- Email field (optional)\n- Password validation (minimum 8 characters)\n- Password confirmation matching\n- On submit:\n  - Creates Supabase Auth user with email (or placeholder format: `{username}@placeholder.local`)\n  - Passes `full_name` in user metadata\n  - Sends verification email if email provided\n  - Shows success message\n\n**Username Availability Check:**\nLocated at `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/api/auth/check-username/route.ts`\n\n- Queries `profiles` table for existing username (case-insensitive)\n- Returns `{ available: boolean }`\n- Minimum 2 character validation\n- Handles non-existent table gracefully (treats as available)\n\n#### Login Flow\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/login-form.tsx`\n\nFeatures:\n- Flexible identifier field (username or email)\n- Email regex validation for detection\n- If identifier is username:\n  - Queries `profiles` table to find user by full_name\n  - Converts to placeholder email format for authentication\n- Supabase password authentication via `signInWithPassword()`\n- Google OAuth integration:\n  - Provider: \"google\"\n  - Redirect: `/auth/callback`\n- Error handling for invalid credentials and user not found\n\n#### OAuth Callback\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/auth/callback/route.ts`\n\n- Handles authorization code from OAuth provider\n- Exchanges code for session via `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code)`\n- Redirects to home page on success (Spanish locale default)\n- Redirects with error query param on failure\n\n### 5. Login/Registration Pages\n\n**Registration Page:**\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/register/page.tsx` (wrapper)\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/register/register-content.tsx` (client component)\n- Centered card layout\n- Link to login page for existing users\n- Uses `RegistrationForm` component\n\n**Login Page:**\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/login/page.tsx` (wrapper)\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/login/login-content.tsx` (client component)\n- Centered card layout\n- Google OAuth button below credentials form\n- Link to registration page for new users\n- Uses `LoginForm` component\n\n### 6. UI Components\n\n**Form Components:**\n- `/src/components/ui/button.tsx` - Button component\n- `/src/components/ui/input.tsx` - Input field component\n- `/src/components/ui/form.tsx` - Form wrapper with validation display\n- `/src/components/ui/label.tsx` - Label component\n\n**Auth Components:**\n- `/src/components/login-form.tsx` - Full login form with validation\n- `/src/components/registration-form.tsx` - Full registration form with username checking\n\n### 7. Header Integration\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/header.tsx`\n\nCurrently has a TODO comment:\n```typescript\n// TODO: Replace with actual auth state from Supabase\nconst isAuthenticated = false;\n```\n\n**Current Auth UI:**\n- Shows \"Log in\" and \"Register\" buttons when not authenticated\n- Would show \"Profile\" link when authenticated\n- Responsive design (desktop nav, mobile menu)\n- Includes language switcher\n\n### 8. Internationalization\n\n**Supported Languages:** Spanish (es), English (en)\n\n**Auth-Related Translations:**\n- Login: titles, field labels, error messages, success messages\n- Registration: account creation prompts, username validation feedback\n- General auth: login/logout/register/profile labels\n\n**Files:**\n- `/messages/en.json` - English translations\n- `/messages/es.json` - Spanish translations\n\n### 9. Tech Stack\n\n**Key Dependencies:**\n- Next.js 16.1.6 (App Router)\n- React 19.2.3\n- @supabase/supabase-js 2.93.3\n- react-hook-form 7.71.1 - Form state management\n- zod 4.3.6 - Schema validation\n- @hookform/resolvers 5.2.2 - Zod integration with react-hook-form\n- next-intl 4.8.2 - Internationalization\n- Tailwind CSS 4 - Styling\n- lucide-react 0.563.0 - Icons\n\n### 10. Auth State Management\n\n**Current Status:** No global auth context implemented\n\nThe authentication state is managed locally:\n- Login form: manages submission state, errors, success\n- Registration form: manages submission state, username availability, errors\n- Header: has hardcoded `isAuthenticated = false` with TODO\n\n**Missing:** Global auth context provider for checking user session and handling auth state across the app\n\n### 11. Key Implementation Details\n\n**Username Logic:**\n- Stored as `full_name` in profiles table\n- Case-insensitive querying (using `ilike`)\n- Unique constraint enforced at database level\n- Placeholder email pattern for users without real email: `{username}@placeholder.local`\n\n**Security:**\n- RLS policies restrict profile access\n- Supabase auth handles password hashing\n- Email verification optional but supported\n- Public read access to profiles table only for username uniqueness checks\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Graceful handling when profiles table doesn't exist (migration not run)\n- User-friendly error messages in multiple languages\n- Network error fallback (allows form submission server-side validates)\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive authentication system is production-ready for basic login/registration flows, with room for enhancement in areas like session management, auth state globalization, and additional OAuth providers."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a58641e (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf186ce8-bbc8-474d-8394-9852a20e107e","uuid":"b379d77c-24cf-4666-bcb0-526a160cf53a","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase to understand the current authentication implementation. I need to understand:\n1. How authentication is currently set up (Supabase configuration, auth context, login components)\n2. The login page structure and components\n3. How user registration works (especially username uniqueness)\n4. The overall project structure for auth-related files\n\nFocus on finding:\n- Auth configuration files\n- Login/registration components\n- Auth context or hooks\n- Any existing OAuth setup\n- Username validation logic","agentId":"a58641e","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I now have a comprehensive understanding of the authentication implementation. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Authentication Implementation Overview\n\nI've explored your codebase thoroughly. Here's a detailed breakdown of the current authentication setup:\n\n### 1. Project Structure\n\n**Key Directories:**\n- `/src/app/[locale]/login/` - Login page components\n- `/src/app/[locale]/register/` - Registration page components\n- `/src/app/api/auth/check-username/` - Username validation API\n- `/src/app/auth/callback/` - OAuth callback handler\n- `/src/lib/supabase.ts` - Supabase client configuration\n- `/src/components/` - Reusable form components (LoginForm, RegistrationForm)\n- `/supabase/migrations/` - Database schema and setup\n- `/messages/` - Translation files (en.json, es.json)\n\n### 2. Supabase Configuration\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/lib/supabase.ts`\n\nThe Supabase client is initialized with public environment variables:\n- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` - Supabase project URL\n- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` - Anonymous public key\n\nCurrently configured for local development at `http://127.0.0.1:54321` with demo credentials in `.env.local`.\n\n### 3. Database Schema\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202000000_create_profiles_table.sql`\n\n**Profiles Table Structure:**\n```sql\n- id (UUID, references auth.users, primary key)\n- full_name (TEXT, NOT NULL, UNIQUE) - serves as username\n- email (TEXT, optional)\n- created_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)\n- updated_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Row Level Security (RLS) enabled\n- Policies for user profile access (users can view/update own profiles)\n- Public read access for username uniqueness checks\n- Automatic profile creation via trigger on user signup\n- Index on `lower(full_name)` for case-insensitive username lookups\n- Automatic `updated_at` timestamp updates via trigger\n\n### 4. Authentication Flow\n\n#### Registration Flow\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/registration-form.tsx`\n\nFeatures:\n- Form validation using React Hook Form + Zod\n- Full Name (username) validation:\n  - 2-100 characters required\n  - Real-time availability checking with debounce (500ms)\n  - Visual feedback (checking, available, taken icons)\n- Email field (optional)\n- Password validation (minimum 8 characters)\n- Password confirmation matching\n- On submit:\n  - Creates Supabase Auth user with email (or placeholder format: `{username}@placeholder.local`)\n  - Passes `full_name` in user metadata\n  - Sends verification email if email provided\n  - Shows success message\n\n**Username Availability Check:**\nLocated at `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/api/auth/check-username/route.ts`\n\n- Queries `profiles` table for existing username (case-insensitive)\n- Returns `{ available: boolean }`\n- Minimum 2 character validation\n- Handles non-existent table gracefully (treats as available)\n\n#### Login Flow\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/login-form.tsx`\n\nFeatures:\n- Flexible identifier field (username or email)\n- Email regex validation for detection\n- If identifier is username:\n  - Queries `profiles` table to find user by full_name\n  - Converts to placeholder email format for authentication\n- Supabase password authentication via `signInWithPassword()`\n- Google OAuth integration:\n  - Provider: \"google\"\n  - Redirect: `/auth/callback`\n- Error handling for invalid credentials and user not found\n\n#### OAuth Callback\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/auth/callback/route.ts`\n\n- Handles authorization code from OAuth provider\n- Exchanges code for session via `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code)`\n- Redirects to home page on success (Spanish locale default)\n- Redirects with error query param on failure\n\n### 5. Login/Registration Pages\n\n**Registration Page:**\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/register/page.tsx` (wrapper)\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/register/register-content.tsx` (client component)\n- Centered card layout\n- Link to login page for existing users\n- Uses `RegistrationForm` component\n\n**Login Page:**\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/login/page.tsx` (wrapper)\n- **File:** `/src/app/[locale]/login/login-content.tsx` (client component)\n- Centered card layout\n- Google OAuth button below credentials form\n- Link to registration page for new users\n- Uses `LoginForm` component\n\n### 6. UI Components\n\n**Form Components:**\n- `/src/components/ui/button.tsx` - Button component\n- `/src/components/ui/input.tsx` - Input field component\n- `/src/components/ui/form.tsx` - Form wrapper with validation display\n- `/src/components/ui/label.tsx` - Label component\n\n**Auth Components:**\n- `/src/components/login-form.tsx` - Full login form with validation\n- `/src/components/registration-form.tsx` - Full registration form with username checking\n\n### 7. Header Integration\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/header.tsx`\n\nCurrently has a TODO comment:\n```typescript\n// TODO: Replace with actual auth state from Supabase\nconst isAuthenticated = false;\n```\n\n**Current Auth UI:**\n- Shows \"Log in\" and \"Register\" buttons when not authenticated\n- Would show \"Profile\" link when authenticated\n- Responsive design (desktop nav, mobile menu)\n- Includes language switcher\n\n### 8. Internationalization\n\n**Supported Languages:** Spanish (es), English (en)\n\n**Auth-Related Translations:**\n- Login: titles, field labels, error messages, success messages\n- Registration: account creation prompts, username validation feedback\n- General auth: login/logout/register/profile labels\n\n**Files:**\n- `/messages/en.json` - English translations\n- `/messages/es.json` - Spanish translations\n\n### 9. Tech Stack\n\n**Key Dependencies:**\n- Next.js 16.1.6 (App Router)\n- React 19.2.3\n- @supabase/supabase-js 2.93.3\n- react-hook-form 7.71.1 - Form state management\n- zod 4.3.6 - Schema validation\n- @hookform/resolvers 5.2.2 - Zod integration with react-hook-form\n- next-intl 4.8.2 - Internationalization\n- Tailwind CSS 4 - Styling\n- lucide-react 0.563.0 - Icons\n\n### 10. Auth State Management\n\n**Current Status:** No global auth context implemented\n\nThe authentication state is managed locally:\n- Login form: manages submission state, errors, success\n- Registration form: manages submission state, username availability, errors\n- Header: has hardcoded `isAuthenticated = false` with TODO\n\n**Missing:** Global auth context provider for checking user session and handling auth state across the app\n\n### 11. Key Implementation Details\n\n**Username Logic:**\n- Stored as `full_name` in profiles table\n- Case-insensitive querying (using `ilike`)\n- Unique constraint enforced at database level\n- Placeholder email pattern for users without real email: `{username}@placeholder.local`\n\n**Security:**\n- RLS policies restrict profile access\n- Supabase auth handles password hashing\n- Email verification optional but supported\n- Public read access to profiles table only for username uniqueness checks\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Graceful handling when profiles table doesn't exist (migration not run)\n- User-friendly error messages in multiple languages\n- Network error fallback (allows form submission server-side validates)\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive authentication system is production-ready for basic login/registration flows, with room for enhancement in areas like session management, auth state globalization, and additional OAuth providers."}],"totalDurationMs":51770,"totalTokens":58650,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":57631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1013},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
